==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 4.67 seconds<sup>140f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*10 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Henry]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
**2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**6 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**1 [[Loris]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Yet another stage featuring the infamous Henry. This time, Loris is here to [[Curse]] your Units and Ragin' Gory appears to push through your defenses. Luring is less optimal as Loris would snipe your base and an unexpected Sir Rel could come along and damage your base. However, it can be used as a last resort. Units with high speed are helpful here to get through Henry and Loris' blindspots.

The main strategy is to save up as much money as possible during the start. Use [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to take out the Ragin' Gories and Sir Rels, and since he's slow, hitting the base will take longer, allowing you to save up money. Hit the base with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to instantly chunk the opening enemies, then try to keep him alive as long as possible to burst down Henry. Other fast Melee attackers like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] will help immensely.

Even if you fail to keep Bahamut alive, the boss wave will be severely crippled beyond repair, so you can pick the rest of the enemies off at a leisurely pace with Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]

==Trivia==
*Going along with the theme of meat and cooking in [[Rose-Colored Road]], ''lamp'' shares a Japanese pronunciation with ''rump'', as in meat cut from the rump of an animal.

